  "description": "The first open gaps: 80, 90 and 100 units wide, and falling in ends the run. The tyre walls and signs mark each lip. Ride at the kicker with steady speed, keep the bike level in the air and land on the downslope beyond. Each landing sits a little lower than the takeoff, so speed is enough; don't brake on the lip.",
